<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Prilep</h1><p class="st-meta">1371 CE – 1395 CE · capital Prilep</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Western Macedonian realm of King Vukašin and his son Marko, whose life as an Ottoman vassal inspired the hero of South Slav epic poetry.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vukasin-mrnjavcevic">Vukašin Mrnjavčević</a>, a Serbian noble, was crowned king in 1365 as co-ruler with Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-uros-v">Uroš V</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/serbian-empire">Serbian Empire</a>, ruling lands in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macedonia-region">Macedonia</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prilep">Prilep</a>. With his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jovan-uglesa">Jovan Uglješa</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/despotate-of-serres">Despotate of Serres</a> he led the campaign against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> in 1371.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vukasin-mrnjavcevic">Vukašin</a> was killed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maritsa">Maritsa</a> in 1371, his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-marko">Marko</a> inherited the royal title and a much smaller realm around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prilep">Prilep</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ohrid">Ohrid</a> and the Pelagonian plain. Marko became an Ottoman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a>, minted coins and completed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/markos-monastery">Marko's Monastery</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skopje">Skopje</a>, begun by his father. His neighbours took Ohrid and other lands.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-marko">Marko</a> died fighting for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mircea-the-elder">Mircea the Elder of Wallachia</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-rovine">Rovine</a> in 1395, and his lands were annexed by the Ottomans. As Kraljević Marko, he became the best-loved hero of Serbian, Macedonian and Bulgarian folk epic.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-prilep.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Prilep" width="320" height="409"><figcaption>Image: PANONIAN; derivative work by Mladifilozof · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kingdom_of_Prilep.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1371 CE – 1395 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Prilep</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Vukašin, Marko</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Serbian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/north-macedonia">North Macedonia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Realm of King Marko, Mrnjavčević lands</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1383&amp;focus=kingdom-of-prilep" aria-label="Kingdom of Prilep on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5206 703 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Prilep lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5526 959L5521 939M5526 959L5709 970"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5521 939h0M5709 970h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5526 959h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5526 959h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Prilep. <a href="/atlas?year=1383&amp;focus=kingdom-of-prilep">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
